#!/bin/bash
java -jar bx-agent/target/bx-agent-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar \
  -s examples/gantt2cpm/Gantt.ecore \
  -t examples/gantt2cpm/CPM.ecore \
  -o generated \
  -e incrementalID \
  -d "Transform a Gantt project diagram (GanttDiagram with Activities and Dependencies) into a CPM (Critical Path Method) network (CPMNetwork). The root name is preserved. Both gantt.Activity and gantt.Dependency map to cpm.Activity (same target type, m:1 mapping): a gantt.Activity maps to a cpm.Activity with the same name and duration; a gantt.Dependency maps to a cpm.Activity whose name is formed by concatenating predecessor.name + \"->\" + successor.name (ASCII arrow, not Unicode), and whose duration equals the offset. In the backward direction, a cpm.Activity whose name contains \"->\" maps back to a gantt.Dependency (backwardCondition: target.getName().contains(\"->\"), offset recovered from duration); all others map back to a gantt.Activity (backwardCondition: !target.getName().contains(\"->\")). gantt.Dependency has no name attribute in the source metamodel, so the name mapping for Dependency is forward-only: sourceAttr must be null or empty string, backwardExpression must be null. The containment reference GanttDiagram.elements / CPMNetwork.elements uses abstract Element as sourceRefTargetType and targetRefTargetType so that both Activities and Dependencies are traversed. cpm.Events have no counterpart in the Gantt model — do not create a typeMapping for Event. The creation of cpm.Events and their wiring to cpm.Activities via sourceEvent/targetEvent (based on DependencyType: StartStart shares predecessor sourceEvent, EndStart shares predecessor targetEvent, StartEnd shares predecessor sourceEvent targeting successor targetEvent, EndEnd shares predecessor targetEvent) must be listed as unresolvedMappings. The backward reconstruction of gantt.Dependency.predecessor, successor and dependencyType from CPM event topology must also be listed as unresolvedMappings. Do not include referenceMappings for predecessor, successor, outgoingDependencies or incomingDependencies."
